      },
      "message": "feat(kernel): heal seam op and solidcore native-format importer corpus\n\nM12.1 stage 3 of the retirement gate. The Kernel seam gains heal():\nsolidcore runs the port's api_heal_brep and the seam judges the result\n(empty and non-positive-tolerance input refused up front; integrity,\nclosed manifold, positive measure and a vertex-edge gap under\nHEAL_GAP_LIMIT afterwards); truck answers Unsupported. New\nsolidcore_import module: the port's native ASCII B-rep format as\nwrite_smb / read_smb / import_smb (read, heal, check).\n\nBench: heal and the native round trip hold five fixtures to their\nclosed forms; a vertex-gap fixture shows the port heals any gap by\ngrowing tolerance, so the seam caps it; a 21-file corrupt corpus, every\ncase under a 60 s time bound, pins raw-reader and importer verdicts.\nFindings pinned: the raw reader returns Ok-empty for garbage files and\nOk for a 1.0 vertex gap; the importer refuses all of them.\n\nNo production path switched; truck keeps its kernel role.\n\nRefs #27\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
