      },
      "message": "fix(kernel): review round on the heal/import seam (#27 stage 3)\n\n- heal_refuses_nonsense_brep_tolerance pins the heal tolerance guard\n  (0, -1, NaN, +inf) under the 60 s bound; the open-sheet check can no\n  longer skip.\n- import_smb returns Imported { brep, notes }: a zone tolerance the\n  reader replaced or clamped is an ImportNote, pinned in the corpus;\n  intact files are asserted against the exact 10-box (bbox too).\n- read_smb refuses a format version newer than the port's (42) and a\n  non-finite declared zone tolerance.\n- vertex_gaps returns VertexGaps and counts edges with no 3D curve; the\n  importer refuses any unjudged edge.\n- HEAL_GAP_LIMIT documented in mm as a chosen bench limit; provenance\n  names the .smb knowledge source; decision 5a records that the port\n  bounds allocations from declared counts (new corpus file: control\n  point count 1e15).\n\nRefs #27\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
